## ADR-006: Explicit save confirmation, no auto-save

**Status:** Accepted

**Context.** Double-click is an ambiguous gesture (also used for text selection), and
machine translations are sometimes wrong.

**Decision.** Double-click shows the translation preview; the word is stored only after
the user clicks "Save". Duplicates are detected (word + translation) and reported inline.

**Consequences.**
- (+) No list pollution from accidental double-clicks.
- (+) User sees and implicitly vets the translation before committing it.
- (−) One extra click per word — judged worthwhile; could be made optional later.

