## ADR-009: Lazy schema migration — cards without `box` are "new"

**Status:** Accepted

**Context.** The SRS feature shipped after users had already saved words. A one-off data
migration in an extension is awkward (no reliable "run once on update" hook across all
clients).

**Decision.** Review fields (`box`, `weight`, `due`, `correct`, `wrong`) are optional.
`box === undefined` means "new card". All consumers (queue builder, badge, popup,
highlights) share this convention.

**Consequences.**
- (+) Zero migration risk; old and new data coexist; the convention survives storage sync
  across devices regardless of which device updates first.
- (−) The `isNew` check is duplicated in several places — must stay consistent. Accepted;
  it's a two-line convention.

